@@ -9,6 +9,17 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+Visited main views stay mounted inside a persistent Astro container. Returning
+to a view reuses its DOM, input values, and React state; inactive views are hidden
+and inert. The cache holds up to eight views and evicts the least recently used
+view. Paths and query strings identify views, while fragments share a view.
+Same-view refreshes use fresh content, and committed router form submissions
+invalidate the cache. A full page reload clears it. Navigation still fetches the
+destination so Astro can update the header, metadata, styles, and history.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for automated DOM lifecycle tests and `pnpm build` for the
+production build.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
